From 9b2f9d6c9c6a4e0a8f1c2d3e4b5a697887766554 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cappy Ishihara <cappy@cappuchino.xyz>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: tg5050: disable unused Vivante NPU binding

The A523 NPU is described with the generic vivante,gc compatible, which
causes the Etnaviv DRM driver to bind to it and expose a second DRM card.
The current Etnaviv path then NULL-dereferences when a DRM client opens
that card. The TG5050 uses Panfrost for its Mali GPU and has no Etnaviv
consumer, so leave the NPU node disabled until a correct NPU driver exists.

Signed-off-by: Cappy Ishihara <cappy@cappuchino.xyz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a523.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a523.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a523.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a523.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a523.dtsi
@@ -1111,0 +1111,1 @@
+			status = "disabled";
-- 
2.51.0
